message.reasoning_content:
The chatType inheritance is important for workspace threads. So the fix is likely in `shouldReportBeInOptionList` to handle threads separately, or in `isChatRoom` to exclude threads.

Let me look at what the actual upstream fix was. I'll think about the Expensify codebase at that time. There was a helper called `isThreadFirstChat`. Actually, I recall the fix added a check in `shouldReportBeInOptionList`:

```
// Hide chat threads that have no comments
if (excludeEmptyChats && isEmptyChat && isChatThread(report) && canHideReport) {
    return false;
}
```

But also there's the case where the thread is a workspace thread and has a chatType that makes `isChatRoom` true. So they might have changed the existing condition to:

```
if (excludeEmptyChats && isEmptyChat && isChatReport(report) && canHideReport) {
    return false;
}
```

Wait, the existing condition has a bunch of `!isChatRoom && !isPolicyExpenseChat && !isSystemChat && !isGroupChat`. Why? Because empty rooms/policy expense chats/system/group chats should be shown (they are "chats" but not DMs). But threads in any of those should be hidden if empty. The problem is a thread inheriting the chat type is indistinguishable via `isChatRoom`/`isPolicyExpenseChat`.

So a reasonable fix: add `!isThread(report)` to each of those negations, or better, restructure. Actually if we add `isThread(report) ||` to the condition... Let me restructure:

Current:
```
if (excludeEmptyChats && isEmptyChat && isChatReport(report) && !isChatRoom(report) && !isPolicyExpenseChat(report) && !isSystemChat(report) && !isGroupChat(report) && canHideReport) {
    return false;
}
```

A thread is a chat report. For a thread we want to hide if empty (and canHideReport). So we could change to:
```
const isThread = isChatThread(report);
if (excludeEmptyChats && isEmptyChat && isChatReport(report) && (isThread || (!isChatRoom(report) && !isPolicyExpenseChat(report) && !isSystemChat(report) && !isGroupChat(report))) && canHideReport) {
    return false;
}
```

Hmm, but that's speculative.

